KNOWNBUG libstdcxx
main.cpp
--cpp20 --object-bits 12
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ defaulted three-way comparison: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
`a < b' is rewritten to (a <=> b) < 0; `a == b' uses the operator== that
a defaulted operator<=> implicitly declares ([class.compare.default]/4),
which CBMC did not declare: "no comparison operator for an operand of
class type" (cpp20_defaulted_spaceship_declares_equality).
